= <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> Leader Isen Glade's Orcish Ancestry Exposed

Linus Aldermere from the Heartland Ministry of the Interior has approached the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> and informed us about three letters written by <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> leader Isen Glade to Axton nerve specialist Corvin Halle during his self-imposed exile in the southern reaches. These letters, confiscated by the Heartland state police, are notable not for their political content but for Glade’s candid discussions of his orcish ancestry—and of the lengths he went to falsify his lineage records to conceal it, potentially exposing him to prosecution for fraud.

Whispers of orcish blood have long dogged Glade, and Gallax has always waved them away. He has faced challenges under the Bloodright Statute before—the law barring those of falsified or impure lineage from high office—but none have ever stuck. This time, we have definitive proof.

What shall be our next move regarding these letters?

> *"We oppose the disgraceful Bloodright Statute wherever we can; we must not join the choir of those who would banish a man from society over the blood in his veins".*

 - The Brocksby, Commonwealth weekly magazine

- @expose_rohm: We will publish the letters, as the revelation that such a high-ranking <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> official carries orcish blood will undoubtedly harm their appeal among their blood-purist core.
- @no_expose_rohm: The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> stands against the Bloodright Statute on principle, and it would be in poor taste to hound a man over his ancestry.

@expose_rohm
on-arrival: dufour_angry_bruning -= 10; guild_royalist -= 2; landed_royalist -= 2; faithful_royalist -= 2; burgher_marcher -= 0.01; unionist_relation += 3; left_dissent += 5

We have published the Glade letters under the title *The Glade Affair*, distributing the pamphlet across all corners of the Commonwealth. This has damaged the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> Party’s appeal among its more blood-purist supporters and has even sparked a plot among some <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> members to murder Glade.

The pamphlet turns the Royalists' own creed back upon them: a party that vows to "cleanse the realm of tainted blood" has knowingly seated a man of orcish descent at its very summit—and forged his lineage records to keep him there. By their own doctrine, it argues, they stand condemned as frauds and hypocrites, no fit guardians of the bloodlines they claim to defend.

Despite this, Gallax has swiftly come to Glade’s defense, publicly reaffirming his position as leader of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>. The electoral performance of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> remains largely unaffected, but the impression this controversy leaves on President DuFour may yet prove significant.

Meanwhile, the pamphlet’s publisher, Aldous Brock, has been brutally beaten by <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> deputies inside the Assembly building as an act of revenge—an event that has overshadowed the scandal itself.

- @persecute_rohm: Attempt to prosecute Glade! Falsifying one's lineage is a crime under the Bloodright Statute, giving us grounds to open legal action against him.

@no_expose_rohm
on-arrival: guild_royalist -= 2; left_dissent -= 5; wholesome_point += 1; rohm_join_banner_time = time + 6

It would be in poor taste for a party that opposes the Bloodright Statute to hound a man over the blood in his veins—the Commonwealth long ago made its peace with whom a man loves, and we will not trade one bigotry for another. We’ve taken the high road, but many within our party feel we’ve missed an opportunity.

@persecute_rohm
achievement: heuchelei
unavailable-subtitle: Despite the widespread distaste for falsified blood-records, the judiciary is too reactionary to be able to convict a top <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span>.
choose-if: judicial_reform >= 3
on-arrival: rohm_explode = 1; burgher_royalist -= 2; guild_royalist -= 4; landed_royalist -= 2; faithful_royalist -= 4; left_dissent += 3; loyalist_strength *= 0.9; dufour_angry_bruning -= 10

With definitive proof of Glade falsifying his lineage under the Bloodright Statute, we have been able to initiate legal action against him once more. Glade is unable to deny the authenticity of the letters, and many have taken that as confirmation of their legitimacy.

In the end, Glade has been convicted under the Bloodright Statute and sentenced to one year in prison. This has brought the scandal back into the spotlight, severely damaging the public perception of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>.